{"_type":"item","id":"019ed1364d897639a93847c281f95ded","type":"work_item","status":"backlog","title":"B4a — manifest.json (id movie_gen, godot_scene panel, ffmpeg dep note)","description":"Full manifest: plugin_id movie_gen, godot_scene panel (entry_scene + scripts[] whitelist), backend block, host_capabilities grants (credential seam + files), file_extensions, note the runtime dependency on the bundled addons/ffmpeg.","created_at":"2026-06-16T16:14:17","updated_at":"2026-06-16T16:14:17","priority":3,"tags":["manifest","movie-gen","packaging"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ed13407df7829a7cee4eca8883cb4"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ed1365bdc7951b32121f59a829cfb","type":"work_item","status":"backlog","title":"B4b — [GitHub Actions] registry + release (reuses A4b pipeline)","description":"In imrans-lab/minerva-plugins. Reuse the shared GHA pipeline landed in A4b: cross-build movie_gen backend (linux/macos/windows), add to regen_registry.py PLUGIN_DIRS allow-list, registry.json entry + tag/tarball/sha256 + 302 URLs. Update the core CI tool-count guard for minerva_movie_gen_*.","created_at":"2026-06-16T16:14:21","updated_at":"2026-06-16T16:14:21","priority":2,"tags":["github-actions","marketplace","movie-gen","registry"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ed13407df7829a7cee4eca8883cb4"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ed1366604726da3cfabc7ee1efc12","type":"work_item","status":"backlog","title":"B4c — Functional test + marketplace-install HITL (FFmpeg playback)","description":"e2e: text_to_video + flf2v through the INSTALLED plugin (ffprobe structural + flf2v endpoint-honoring check). Clean-profile marketplace_install HITL: advertises, installs, panel opens, minerva_movie_gen_* tools register, and the mp4 plays in-panel via FFmpegVideoStream.","created_at":"2026-06-16T16:14:23","updated_at":"2026-06-16T16:14:23","priority":3,"tags":["hitl","marketplace","movie-gen","test"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ed13407df7829a7cee4eca8883cb4"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ed79f0cce7902bd096d68b5e98d45","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"Agent-driven media-gen artifacts surface in the UI by default (background opt-out)","description":"GAP (found 2026-06-17 HITL): calling minerva_movie_gen_i2v (and flf2v/text_to_video, and the gen3d tools) directly over MCP returns the artifact PATH to the caller but nothing surfaces in the Minerva UI — the user sees nothing. Only the panel renders videos, and only ones IT generated. This violates the \"MCP drives all tasks WITH UI feedback\" + \"silent MCP runs are unacceptable\" principles. Sibling to the job-state-visibility gap (movie_gen publishes no plugin_state).\n\nDESIGN (owner-approved):\n- DEFAULT = visible: after a successful gen, the plugin surfaces the artifact in the UI. v1 surface = os_open via mcp.proxy:minerva_os_open (subject to OSOpenPolicy) — consistent with O1's non-PNG artifact path. Richer in-app viewer is the existing deferred follow-up 019ecd3d68bc.\n- OPT-OUT = a `background: bool` tool param (default false). When true, skip surfacing and just return the path — so an agent can do e.g. generate → copy to ~/temp/upload_funny_cat.mp4 → upload, with no UI noise.\n- The PANEL passes background:true on its own generate calls (it already previews inline; avoid double-surfacing).\n\nSCOPE: movie-gen backend (surface helper requesting mcp.proxy:minerva_os_open, mirrors the fetch_credentials/request_capability pattern; `background` arg in all 3 handlers + tools/list), manifest (grant mcp.proxy:minerva_os_open + `background` param), panel (send background:true). Generalize the same pattern to gen3d (GLB → os_open). \n\nFUTURE: option 3 (push-to-open-panel event so an open panel previews agent-driven gens) and the in-app viewer (019ecd3d68bc) are richer surfaces; os_open is the reliable v1.","created_at":"2026-06-17T22:06:25","updated_at":"2026-06-17T23:35:38","priority":2,"tags":["3d-gen","mcp-visibility","media-gen","movie-gen","ux"],"resolution":"completed"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec","type":"dcr","status":"shipped","title":"Drive plugin — cloud-canonical multi-device sync for Minerva projects (Problem A)","description":"GOAL: Ship a new \"drive\" marketplace plugin that synchronizes Minerva project files (.minproj, and arbitrary files) across one owner's devices (Windows/Linux/Mac), surviving multi-machine edits without losing an edit. SCOPE = single-owner multi-device (Problem A). Share-by-invitation to other people (Problem B) is EXPLICITLY OUT OF SCOPE.\n\nARCHITECTURE (cloud-canonical, pure plugin — verified against the live deployed surface):\n- Content blobs -> deployed artifact-service (artifact/upload visibility=private, download, list-mine; per-user JWT-ENFORCED, owner-only delete). Each save = a new immutable blob (new artifact:// URI). \"Current\" = newest blob per proj_uuid; older blobs = recoverable history.\n- Manifest/index derived from list-mine via artifact tags {proj_uuid, version, parent_version, content_hash, device, mtime}. (Optional agent-history JSON index only if scan cost grows — not in this DCR.)\n- Liveness -> Core pub/sub topic drive/<user>/changed; periodic list-mine poll as fallback.\n- Auth/transport -> host.core.session mints {ws_url, token, client_id}; the plugin opens its OWN Core WebSocket and acts as the user (svc_allow scoped). CONFIRMED: zero Minerva-core and zero minervaservices changes for Problem A.\n- Conflict model: last-writer-wins on the \"current\" pointer + conflict-copies on divergence (compare local base_version vs cloud current). GUARANTEE: never loses an edit; may emit a conflict-copy for the user to reconcile. No CRDT/OT.\n\nDELIVERY (marketplace pipeline, the \"plugin store\"): CI -> per-platform binary -> registry -> install. New files under drive/ (manifest.json, Cargo.toml, src/main.rs, .gitignore, ui/). New .github/workflows/drive.yml build+release matrix (linux-x86_64, macos-universal, windows-x86_64). Add \"drive\" to scripts/regen_registry.py PLUGIN_DIRS (alphabetical). Conventions: release tag drive-v<semver>; tarball drive-<ver>-<target>.tar.gz; binary name drive-plugin (must match manifest entrypoint); tool names minerva_drive_*; panel script class_name prefix Drive_.\n\nDRY DECISION (controlled): minerva-media-client is media-gen-specific (binary frame relay; NO artifact upload/list-mine/pubsub). Drive builds a minimal generic core/artifact client as ONE clean module inside its own crate, reusing the host.core.session credential pattern + Core register handshake by reference. Do NOT create a new shared crate in this DCR (scope creep); structure the module so it COULD be promoted to shared later.\n\nBINDING RISK CONTROLS (apply to every implementation task; verified by cold-Opus review):\n1) WRONG BASE COMMIT — branch dcr/drive off minerva-plugins `main` HEAD; each task records its base and verifies (git log) before any edit.\n2) POOR DRY — exactly one core/artifact-client module and one sync engine; tool/panel layers are thin wrappers; Explore preflight to find reuse; reviewer rejects any duplicated transport/sync logic.\n3) PM-IN-CODE — code comments describe FUNCTIONALITY only. No DCR ids, ticket/PLG refs, \"user requested\", or meta-comments (\"this comment should...\"). Enforced by a deterministic grep gate in every cold review (standard = KB 019eeda99ff6).\n4) SCOPE CREEP — allowed-files list per task; OUT: Problem B, any new shared crate, any Minerva-core or minervaservices change, one-click in-app project open (MVP writes .minproj to disk + notifies). Reviewer verifies only allowed files changed.\n\nEXECUTION + SUB-AGENT PLAN: see child work_item and its task children. Reviews are cold-Opus (fresh context) running a Tier-A grep gate (comment hygiene + correct base branch + allowed-files-only + duplication scan) then Tier-B judgment.","created_at":"2026-06-22T21:53:53","updated_at":"2026-06-23T22:29:41","tags":["drive","marketplace","plugin","sync"]}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef153b6af78cebf99b84f20339d0b","type":"work_item","status":"backlog","title":"Build &amp; ship drive plugin (Problem A) — execution plan","description":"Implements the parent DCR. Two-repo base discipline: PLUGIN work lands directly on minerva-plugins `main` (owner directive — no dcr/drive branch); CORE work lands on Minerva `development`. Verify the right repo+base before each task. Tasks are the work_item children below.\n\n=== PHASE 1 (MVP, Problem A) — DONE & committed on minerva-plugins main (afc1375..a69efd3) ===\nT1 scaffold+CI, T2 artifact client (proven live), T3 sync+conflict engine, T4 status/list/sync tools, T5 panel, T6 E2E+README, T7 cold-Opus audit (GO). Picker follow-up (work_item 019ef57b, done): minerva_drive_add/remove + registered-paths model. Post-MVP hardening (committed): sync result returns arrays not counts (panel cast crash); list/status made local-first (files show offline/instantly); initial fetch moved to _on_panel_loaded (IPC not attached in _ready); tree rows shown via Tree.hide_root (root.visible=false hid all rows). Live-verified via minerva_drive_list.\n\n=== PHASE 2 (this update) — Consumption + open/save lifecycle (scope the DCR under-specified) ===\nGROUP A — plugin-only consumption (zero-core, Sonnet, parallelizable):\n- T8 Reveal-in-folder + Open-with-OS: panel row actions via mcp.proxy:minerva_os_open (re-add capability to manifest -> REINSTALL). \n- T9 Download-a-copy-to: file_picker(save) + new minerva_drive_export tool writing the current version to a chosen path.\n- T10 Set-Drive-folder in-panel: persisted setting for the pull destination (replaces DRIVE_FOLDER-env-only).\nGROUP B — open/save/sync lifecycle (CORE + Opus-direct; the data-safety heart):\n- T11 Lifecycle design + conflict policy (shaping): pull-on-open, NEVER clobber a file Minerva has open, save->push, base-version (proj_uuid+version) tracking, recent-menu handling. Settles THE decision: stale-base divergence winner (recommended default = the open/local working copy wins the canonical path; cloud parked as conflict copy — pending owner confirm). Output: spec the impl tasks follow.\n- T12 host.project.open core capability (Minerva development): emits SingletonObject.OpenProject(path) (reuses File-menu load incl. save-current prompt); path validation. The in-app-open seam (not exposed today).\n- T13 Open-from-Drive (plugin, uses T12): double-click (Tree.item_activated) + Open button -> pull-latest-then-open; refuse to overwrite a currently-open file (-> conflict copy + review); record loaded base.\n- T14 Save->push + divergence: detect save of a tracked .minproj, push on sync; stale-base divergence -> conflict per T11 policy (assess whether a core save-hook is needed).\n- T15 Open-Recent / recent-menu awareness (Minerva core): route recent-opens of Drive paths through pull-on-open + warning; off-Drive banner \"not synced; cloud may be ahead\".\nGROUP C — gate:\n- T16 cold-Opus audit of Phase 2 = HITL gate.\n\nORCHESTRATION + MODELS (Phase 2): T8/T9/T10 Sonnet (mechanical, plugin-only) — parallel. T11 design = Opus direct (or short Explore preflight of Minerva project lifecycle first). T12/T15 Opus direct (CORE, careful). T13/T14 Opus direct (conflict/data-safety correctness). T16 cold Opus, fresh context.\n\nPARALLELIZATION: T11 design first (barrier — settles policy + seams). Then Lane A (Sonnet) T8/T9/T10 concurrent with Lane B (Opus) T12 -> T13 -> {T14, T15}. T16 audits last.\n\nRISK CONTROLS — same 4 binding controls as the DCR (correct base, DRY, no PM-in-code, no scope creep), PLUS verification additions learned in Phase 1 (every Phase-2 cold review must check these):\n1) CROSS-BOUNDARY VALUE SHAPES: backend tool JSON must match what the panel reads (the sync-payload counts-vs-arrays crash). Add a shape test for any new tool the panel consumes.\n2) GODOT RUNTIME SEMANTICS not caught by parse-check: Tree.hide_root (never root.visible=false), initial IPC fetch in _on_panel_loaded (not _ready), responsive geometry. Reviewer runs/▸reasons about runtime, not just --check-only.\n3) DEPLOY/LIFECYCLE: manifest/permission/ipc changes need REINSTALL not reload; new tools need /mcp reconnect; the binary must be copied beside manifest.json (entrypoint ./drive-plugin). \n4) DATA SAFETY (hard gate): never overwrite a file Minerva has open; never lose an edit (conflict copy); pull-latest-on-open. T16 must prove these.\nTier-A grep gate per review: correct repo+base; allowed-files only; no DCR/ticket/\"user requested\"/meta comments; no duplicated transport/sync/render logic.","created_at":"2026-06-22T21:54:15","updated_at":"2026-06-23T19:53:53","tags":["drive","execution-plan","plugin"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef153fd2079a49ff7dda171ea7040","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T1 — Scaffold + publish wiring (CI-first)","description":"Base: NEW branch dcr/drive off minerva-plugins `main` HEAD (verify with git log before editing). Model/agent: Sonnet via /work-cycle, worktree-isolated. Deps: none (hard barrier — unblocks all other tasks). Mirror the movie-gen plugin exactly.\n\nDO: create the drive plugin scaffold and prove it ships through CI.\nALLOWED FILES (scope fence — touch nothing else):\n- drive/manifest.json (id=\"drive\", name, version 0.0.1, host_api_version, release_targets [linux-x86_64, macos-universal, windows-x86_64], backend.entrypoint ./drive-plugin, permissions.host_capabilities incl host.core.session + host.notify, tools[] stub, ui.panels[] decl, file_extensions/.save_mode if panel)\n- drive/Cargo.toml ([[bin]] name = \"drive-plugin\")\n- drive/src/main.rs (JSON-RPC 2.0 stdio loop: initialize + tools/list returning the manifest tools; stderr logging only)\n- drive/.gitignore (target/, etc.)\n- .github/workflows/drive.yml (build matrix + release job; copy movie-gen.yml, swap ids/paths/tag prefix drive-v*)\n- scripts/regen_registry.py (add \"drive\" to PLUGIN_DIRS, keep alphabetical)\n\nDONE: branch CI builds all 3 targets green (prerelease on branch); registry-check.yml passes (regen_registry.py + git diff --exit-code clean once a tag exists / or no-drift for the untagged branch). No DCR/ticket/meta comments in any file. Cold-Opus review: base branch correct, only allowed files touched, manifest prefix rules satisfied (tool names minerva_drive_*, panel class_name prefix Drive_).","created_at":"2026-06-22T21:54:33","updated_at":"2026-06-22T22:51:38","tags":["T1","ci","drive","scaffold"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef153b6af78cebf99b84f20339d0b"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef154243070f593ed999fdea4e587","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T2 — Core/artifact client module (DRY seam)","description":"Base: dcr/drive (verify). Model/agent: Opus DIRECT (orchestrator) — protocol + DRY critical. Deps: T1 scaffold. Blocks: T3, T4. W0 Explore preflight first: confirm the artifact-service wire shape (request envelope, base64 content, list-mine response) and read minerva-media-client's fetch_credentials + register handshake to reuse the pattern by reference (it is NOT reusable for artifact ops).\n\nDO: build drive/src/core_client.rs (or module) — the ONLY place that talks to Core.\n- credentials: request_capability(\"host.core.session\") -> {ws_url, token, client_id}\n- connect + Core register handshake; request/response correlation by request_id\n- artifact ops: upload(filename, bytes, tags, visibility=private) -> uri; download(uri) -> bytes; list_mine() -> [{uri, filename, tags, ...}]\n- pubsub: subscribe(topic) + a callback/stream for drive/<user>/changed\nALLOWED FILES: drive/src/core_client.rs (+ mod decl in main.rs), drive/Cargo.toml (deps only). Nothing else.\n\nDRY GUARD: no transport/handshake logic anywhere but this module; T3/T4 consume it. DONE: unit tests against a fake Core (no live backend) cover upload/download/list-mine round-trip + subscribe dispatch + error envelopes. Cold-Opus review: single transport seam, no duplication, functionality-only comments, only allowed files.","created_at":"2026-06-22T21:54:43","updated_at":"2026-06-22T22:58:17","tags":["T2","core-client","drive","dry"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef153b6af78cebf99b84f20339d0b"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef15446907e1fbe3adab61941c124","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T3 — Sync + conflict engine (data-safety heart)","description":"Base: dcr/drive (verify). Model/agent: Opus DIRECT — conflict correctness IS the data-loss guarantee. Deps: T2. Blocks: T4, T6.\n\nDO: build drive/src/sync.rs over the T2 core_client.\n- tag schema {proj_uuid, version, parent_version, content_hash, device, mtime}\n- resolve current = newest version per proj_uuid from list_mine\n- push(file): hash; read cloud current; if cloud.version==base -> upload version=base+1 parent=base (fast-forward); else upload as conflict-copy (tag conflict=true, from=device) leaving cloud current authoritative\n- pull(proj): if cloud.version>base and no local dirty -> download+replace+advance base; if dirty -> defer to conflict-on-next-save\n- local per-project state {proj_uuid, current_uri, base_version, content_hash} in plugin data dir\nALLOWED FILES: drive/src/sync.rs (+ mod decl), drive/src/state.rs if needed. NOT core_client.rs (consume it), NOT tools/panel.\n\nDONE: unit tests with a fake core_client prove: clean fast-forward; concurrent divergence -> conflict-copy with BOTH versions retrievable (no data loss); no-CAS race -> at most an extra conflict-copy, never loss. Cold-Opus review: guarantee holds, no transport logic here (DRY), functionality-only comments, only allowed files.","created_at":"2026-06-22T21:54:52","updated_at":"2026-06-22T23:03:04","tags":["T3","conflict","drive","sync"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef153b6af78cebf99b84f20339d0b"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef15460047fb8923a3dedeb78f84b","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T4 — MCP tool surface","description":"Base: dcr/drive (verify). Model/agent: Sonnet (mechanical wrappers). Deps: T3 (tool decls may be drafted alongside T1).\n\nDO: expose the sync engine via MCP tools (the agent-driven surface, per the platform north star).\n- tools: minerva_drive_list, minerva_drive_status, minerva_drive_push, minerva_drive_pull, minerva_drive_open, minerva_drive_resolve_conflict\n- each is a THIN wrapper calling T3; no business logic in the tool layer\nALLOWED FILES: drive/src/main.rs (tools/call dispatch arms), drive/manifest.json (tools[] + input_schema for each). NOT sync.rs/core_client.rs.\n\nDONE: manifest tools[] valid (names minerva_drive_*, schemas declare every arg shape — undeclared nested args get stringified by Minerva); main.rs dispatches each to T3; round-trip works against the fake. Cold-Opus review: wrappers are thin, no duplicated logic, functionality-only comments, only allowed files.","created_at":"2026-06-22T21:54:59","updated_at":"2026-06-22T23:10:33","tags":["T4","drive","mcp-tools"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef153b6af78cebf99b84f20339d0b"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef1547c69799fbebaf8c2f26ca576","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T5 — Panel UI (Godot scene + GDScript)","description":"Base: dcr/drive (verify). Model/agent: Sonnet — mirrors movie_gen ui/. Deps: T1 only (needs the tool-name + ipc_channels contract, not sync internals) — runs in PARALLEL with Lane A (T2/T3).\n\nDO: build drive/ui/ panel.\n- project list with status per item (synced / pending / conflict)\n- open-in-Minerva: write the synced .minproj to disk + host.notify (one-click in-app project open is OUT of scope)\n- conflict resolver: keep-mine / keep-theirs / keep-both, calling minerva_drive_resolve_conflict\n- responsive to the variable editor pane grid (derive geometry from live rect; never hardcode pane dims)\nALLOWED FILES: drive/ui/DrivePanel.tscn, drive/ui/DrivePanel.gd, drive/manifest.json (ui.panels + ipc_messages only). NOT rust src.\n\nDONE: panel loads; class_name prefix Drive_; ipc_channels list the drive tools; status renders from minerva_drive_status; conflict resolver wired. Cold-Opus review: prefix/ipc rules satisfied, responsive layout, functionality-only comments, only allowed files.","created_at":"2026-06-22T21:55:06","updated_at":"2026-06-22T22:58:20","tags":["T5","drive","panel","ui"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef153b6af78cebf99b84f20339d0b"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef154999473cab73c5ea1585ab154","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T6 — End-to-end functional test + docs","description":"Base: dcr/drive (verify). Model/agent: Sonnet. Deps: T3 + T4 + T5.\n\nDO: prove the system end-to-end and document it.\n- functional test: simulate two devices (two local states + one fake/shared artifact store) -> edit on A, sync, pull on B (fast-forward); concurrent edit on A and B -> conflict-copy, BOTH recoverable\n- docs: drive/README.md (what it does, install via marketplace, the never-lose-an-edit guarantee + conflict-copy behavior); a short entry/touch in docs/PLUGIN_DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md if a new pattern is introduced\nALLOWED FILES: drive/tests/** (or src test module), drive/README.md, docs/PLUGIN_DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md (additive). NOT plugin logic.\n\nDONE: functional test green; docs describe the real guarantee (no over-claim — LWW pointer + conflict-copies, not CRDT). Cold-Opus review: test actually exercises divergence, docs match behavior, functionality-only comments, only allowed files.","created_at":"2026-06-22T21:55:13","updated_at":"2026-06-22T23:12:35","tags":["T6","docs","drive","e2e"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef153b6af78cebf99b84f20339d0b"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef154bd877f54a3cdeb48250bfca8","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T7 — Whole-plugin cold-Opus audit (HITL gate)","description":"Base: dcr/drive (verify). Model/agent: cold Opus, fresh context, no prior task memory. Deps: T1-T6 all done.\n\nDO: audit the whole plugin diff against the four binding risk controls and the architecture.\nTIER-A deterministic grep gate (must pass):\n- base: whole branch is dcr/drive off minerva-plugins main HEAD (git log/merge-base)\n- scope: only drive/**, .github/workflows/drive.yml, scripts/regen_registry.py changed; no Minerva-core / minervaservices / shared-crate changes; no Problem-B code\n- PM-in-code: diff has no DCR/ticket/PLG ids, no \"user requested\", no meta-comments\n- DRY: exactly one transport seam (core_client) and one sync engine; no duplication\nTIER-B judgment: conflict logic never loses an edit; manifest prefix/tool rules correct; CI/registry wiring correct (PLUGIN_DIRS, tag convention, tarball name, binary name); docs do not over-claim.\n\nDONE: audit report attached to this item with GO/NO-GO per control. NO-GO items become follow-up tasks. This item's completion = the single HITL gate; merge to main + tag drive-v0.0.1 is the OWNER's action, not part of this DCR.","created_at":"2026-06-22T21:55:23","updated_at":"2026-06-22T23:17:16","tags":["T7","audit","drive","hitl"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef153b6af78cebf99b84f20339d0b"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef1836edf78b1b7cc2418b5ce5a08","type":"hint","status":"draft","title":"artifact-service request envelope (action in topic; client supplies params.user_id)","created_at":"2026-06-22T22:46:23","updated_at":"2026-06-22T22:46:23","tags":["artifact-service","core-ws","drive","wire-format"],"value":"CONFIRMED live (2026-06-22) against prod artifact-service via Core WS. Request envelope: {\"cmd\":\"request\",\"topic\":\"artifact/<action>\",\"entity_type\":\"client\",\"params\":{\"target_service_id\":\"artifact-service\",\"user_id\":\"<sub>\",\"request_id\":\"<uuid>\",\"auth\":\"<jwt>\",\"client_id\":\"<sub>\",\"data\":{...}}}. THREE gotchas: (1) the ACTION goes in `topic` (artifact/upload|download|list-mine|delete|add-metadata|search) — NOT in data, NOT implied by target_service_id alone (wrong topic = silent timeout, no error). (2) The client MUST set params.user_id = the JWT sub / client_id from host.core.session — Core does NOT inject it and data.user_id is IGNORED; omitting it errors \"user_id required (from JWT token)\" even with artifact-service in svc_allow. (3) Response correlates by params.request_id; success at params.result, errors as {\"cmd\":\"error\",\"params\":{\"error\":...}}. list-mine returns params.result.artifacts[] each {artifact_uri, filename, size, description, tags[], framework, language, visibility, uploaded_at, file_exists}. Reproduce with /tmp/drive_wire_smoke.py (mirrors infrastructure/test/simple-discovery-test.py).","component":"artifact-service","key":"wire-contract","confidence":"high","research_cost":3}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef571de8670aca55ba4edb1aa33d1","type":"hint","status":"draft","title":"Local Rust plugin run needs the binary copied beside manifest.json (entrypoint ./<id>-plugin)","created_at":"2026-06-23T17:05:40","updated_at":"2026-06-23T17:05:40","tags":["build","drive","missing-binary","plugins","rust"],"value":"A Rust plugin's manifest entrypoint is \"./<id>-plugin\" (resolved BESIDE manifest.json in the plugin dir). `cargo build --release` only produces target/release/<id>-plugin — Minerva can't find it there and fails to start with a \"missing binary\" error. For LOCAL/dev runs you MUST copy it into place: `cp <plugin>/target/release/<id>-plugin <plugin>/<id>-plugin && chmod +x`. movie-gen keeps movie_gen-plugin beside its manifest for this reason. The binary is gitignored (target/ + the bare name), so it's never committed (FCIB-clean); CI does this copy during tarball packaging. Verify by smoking the ENTRYPOINT path, not target/release: `python3 scripts/smoke/mcp_smoke.py <plugin>/<id>-plugin`. After deploying, reload the plugin AND `/mcp` reconnect (reload alone doesn't refresh the MCP tool registry).","component":"plugins","key":"local-binary-deploy","confidence":"high","research_cost":1}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef57b36e87e099e67513cb4dd3c36","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"Drive: file chooser + register/unregister tracked paths","description":"Follow-up to the shipped MVP: give the user an explicit way to choose what Drive syncs (owner picked the add-file/folder picker model over the magic-folder default). MVP scope = FILES (covers .minproj/projects); folder selection deferred (file_picker exemplar supports file open/save). Changes: SyncState gains a `tracked: Vec<String>` registered-paths set (serde default for back-compat); two new local-only tools minerva_drive_add{path}/minerva_drive_remove{path}; sync/status/list operate over the registered set instead of a drive-folder scan; cloud-only pulls auto-register so they sync back; ProjectStatus carries `path` so the panel can remove by row; panel gets a \"+ Add to sync\" button (host.dialogs.file_picker -> add -> refresh) and a \"Remove selected\" button; manifest re-adds host.dialogs.file_picker + declares the two tools in tools[]/ipc_channels/ipc_messages. Implemented end-to-end by orchestrator (Opus) to keep cross-component shapes consistent after the sync-payload contract-drift bug; add an integration-boundary test for the new shapes + SyncState serde back-compat.","created_at":"2026-06-23T17:15:53","updated_at":"2026-06-23T17:22:41","tags":["drive","picker","ux"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef580b07a7d2f982e91d56ea18070","type":"hint","status":"draft","title":"Parse-check off-tree plugin .gd via temp project + stub base + editor import","created_at":"2026-06-23T17:21:52","updated_at":"2026-06-23T17:21:52","tags":["gdscript","godot","plugins","validation"],"value":"To actually parse/type-check an off-tree plugin GDScript (which `extends MinervaPluginPanel` — a class_name that doesn't resolve standalone, so a bare `godot --check-only --script panel.gd` only ever reports 'Could not find base class'): make a temp project with a STUB base class, import it so the class_name registers, THEN check. Steps: mkdir /tmp/chk; write project.godot; write MinervaPluginPanel.gd = `class_name MinervaPluginPanel extends Control` + any signals/methods the panel uses (e.g. `signal request(channel,args,reply_id)`, `func receive(c,p): pass`); cp the panel in; run `godot --headless --path /tmp/chk --editor --quit-after 3` once to build .godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg; then `godot --headless --path /tmp/chk --check-only --script Panel.gd` → exit 0 = clean full-body parse. The import pass is REQUIRED (without it class_name isn't registered and you only get the base-class error). Godot 4.6 at /usr/local/bin/godot.","component":"godot","key":"parse-check-off-tree-plugin-gd","confidence":"high","research_cost":2}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef5b601ff7fbdbe48418a297958bf","type":"hint","status":"draft","title":"Manifest permission/capability/ipc_messages changes need plugin reinstall, not reload","created_at":"2026-06-23T18:20:06","updated_at":"2026-06-23T18:20:06","tags":["capabilities","drive","permission-denied","plugins","reload"],"value":"Changing a plugin's manifest.json permissions/capabilities (host_capabilities) or ui.ipc_messages/ipc_channels does NOT take effect on a hot reload — the panel capability call fails with \"Permission denied\" (capability_not_granted). Reason: PluginPolicy.get_requested_capabilities reads host_capabilities from the persisted PluginDB record (plugin_db.get_by_id), NOT the live manifest.json. Only PluginManager.install_plugin / update_plugin refresh the DB (via _db.update_definition). Hot reload (_hot_reload_gd/_hot_reload_tscn) only re-reads panel .gd/.tscn — so new UI/buttons appear but manifest grants are stale. FIX: reinstall/update the plugin from its manifest. This is the 3rd facet of \"reload != refresh\": (1) new MCP tools need /mcp reconnect [mcp_plugin_reload_doesnt_refresh_tools], (2) event declarations need reinstall [plugin_event_declaration_stale_db], (3) capability/ipc_messages grants need reinstall (this). Panel capability:* channels must ALSO be in manifest ui.ipc_messages (PluginScenePanelBroker._validate_channel_declared).","component":"plugins","key":"manifest-permission-change-needs-reinstall","confidence":"high","research_cost":2}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef5ca392b746b8b68a4759b44a8a4","type":"hint","status":"draft","title":"Plugin panel initial data fetch belongs in _on_panel_loaded, not _ready (IPC not attached yet)","created_at":"2026-06-23T18:42:11","updated_at":"2026-06-23T18:42:11","tags":["drive","ipc","lifecycle","panel","plugins"],"value":"A godot_scene plugin panel's FIRST IPC/data fetch must run in _on_panel_loaded(ctx), NOT in _ready (even via call_deferred). The host (PluginScenePanelBroker) attaches the $_MinervaIPC helper node during register_panel, which runs AFTER the scene's _ready(); _on_panel_loaded is fired after that. So get_node_or_null('_MinervaIPC') is null during _ready → an initial refresh there silently no-ops and the panel renders empty with no retry (symptom: existing items don't show on panel open, but show after a manual action once IPC exists). Fix: build UI in _ready, call your refresh()/load in _on_panel_loaded. Shipped example: nametag-maker calls _render_current_preview() in _on_panel_loaded. Requests emitted during _on_panel_loaded are trampolined (delivered after it returns), so emitting there is safe. Panel .gd is re-read on next panel OPEN (close+reopen), no reinstall.","component":"plugins","key":"panel-initial-fetch-in-on-panel-loaded","confidence":"high","research_cost":2}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef5d34dd97b6a95fcc64262d7cc8f","type":"hint","status":"draft","title":"Godot Tree: use hide_root=true, never root TreeItem.visible=false (hides all rows)","created_at":"2026-06-23T18:52:06","updated_at":"2026-06-23T18:52:06","tags":["drive","godot","plugins","tree","ui"],"value":"Godot Tree: to hide the synthetic root and show its children as top-level rows, set `tree.hide_root = true`. Do NOT create the root and set `root.visible = false` — TreeItem.visible cascades to ALL descendants, so it hides every row and the Tree looks empty even though items were added. Symptom seen in drive plugin: list returned rows (verified in logs) but panel showed nothing; cause was `root.visible = false` in _populate_tree. Static review/parse-check won't catch this (it's valid GDScript + correct API, wrong semantics) — only runtime shows the empty tree.","component":"godot","key":"tree-hide-root-not-item-visible","confidence":"high","research_cost":3}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef60c91b47748b4078ce0aa636d10","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T8 Drive: Open-with-OS + Reveal-in-folder row actions","description":"Plugin-only (minerva-plugins main). Panel row buttons: \"Open\" = mcp.proxy:minerva_os_open on the file path (OS default handler; interim until the proper in-app open lands in T13); \"Reveal\" = os_open the containing folder. Re-add mcp.proxy:minerva_os_open to manifest host_capabilities + panel ipc_channels (capability:mcp.proxy:minerva_os_open) -> REINSTALL to take effect. Model: Sonnet. Allowed files: drive/ui/DrivePanel.gd, drive/manifest.json. Risks: allowed-files only; no PM-in-code; Godot runtime (button enable on row select). Verify: reinstall, click Open/Reveal on the selected row.","created_at":"2026-06-23T19:54:39","updated_at":"2026-06-23T20:32:55","tags":["drive","phase2","ux"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef60ca6157486a4956fb6bd81b74c","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T9 Drive: Download-a-copy-to (export current version)","description":"Plugin-only (minerva-plugins main). New tool minerva_drive_export{proj_uuid OR path, dest_path} -> downloads the current cloud version bytes (reuse artifact_client.download via the proj's current uri) and writes to dest_path. Panel: row \"Download…\" -> file_picker(save) -> export -> status. Especially for Cloud-only rows (true download, not just pull-into-MinervaDrive). Declare tool in manifest tools[] + panel ipc_channels/ipc_messages. Model: Sonnet. Allowed: drive/src/main.rs, drive/src/sync.rs (a resolve-current-uri helper if needed), drive/manifest.json, drive/ui/DrivePanel.gd. Risks: add a value-shape test for the export tool result; allowed-files only; no PM-in-code; DRY (reuse client/engine, no new transport).","created_at":"2026-06-23T19:54:44","updated_at":"2026-06-23T20:39:01","tags":["drive","phase2","ux"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef60cb6df7d70a52df5925605f588","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T10 Drive: Set Drive folder in-panel","description":"Plugin-only (minerva-plugins main). Persist a drive-folder override (pull destination) in SyncState; tools use state override else DRIVE_FOLDER env else ~/MinervaDrive. Panel: a folder field + picker + Save. Model: Sonnet. Allowed: drive/src/main.rs (drive_folder() consults state), drive/src/sync.rs (SyncState field, serde-default), drive/manifest.json (if a set tool added), drive/ui/DrivePanel.gd. Risks: serde back-compat (default), changing folder doesn't move existing tracked entries (document); allowed-files only; no PM-in-code.","created_at":"2026-06-23T19:54:48","updated_at":"2026-06-23T20:45:16","tags":["drive","phase2","ux"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef60ccd3376059274f251f8655cb5","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T11 Drive: open/save/sync lifecycle design + conflict policy (shaping)","description":"SHAPING (no shipped code). Optional short Explore preflight of Minerva project open/save/recent lifecycle. Produce a spec (docket comment/design note) the impl tasks follow, covering: (1) pull-latest-on-open; (2) NEVER overwrite a file Minerva has open (cloud-newer -> conflict, not clobber) — how Drive learns which files are open; (3) save -> push (core save-hook/event vs hash-on-sync); (4) base-version tracking (proj_uuid+version) on the open project for precise divergence; (5) Open-Recent / File>Open of Drive paths -> pull-on-open + warning, off-Drive banner.\n\nCONFLICT STRATEGY (refined per owner — git-style merge where possible): the cloud-canonical immutable history gives us a COMMON ANCESTOR (the base_version the local edit descended from is still a recoverable blob), so a true 3-WAY MERGE (base + local + cloud) is feasible. Tiered handler:\n- One side changed -> fast-forward (no conflict).\n- Both changed + PLAIN TEXT -> 3-way merge by reusing git's engine (`git merge-file` / `diff3`) on three temp files: auto-merge non-overlapping hunks; on true conflict, write the file with <<<<<<< / ======= / >>>>>>> markers, flag it, let the user resolve in a Minerva editor, then a \"mark resolved & re-sync\" action pushes the merged result. Do NOT reinvent the merge algorithm.\n- Both changed + STRUCTURED/BINARY (.minproj is JSON, possibly zipped) -> conflict-copy (keep both, never lose either); markers would corrupt JSON so they are NOT used here. Future option: SEMANTIC merge of project components (notes/chats/editors) instead of raw bytes — bigger, format-specific, defer.\nResolve files mergeability by extension + binary sniff. This SUPERSEDES the blunt local-wins/cloud-wins question for text; structured/binary keep the safe conflict-copy. DECISION STILL OPEN for .minproj specifically: conflict-copy now vs invest in semantic project merge — recommend conflict-copy in v1, semantic merge as a follow-up.\n\nEnumerate exact Minerva-core seams (informs T12/T15) and which work is plugin vs core. Model: Opus direct. Output gates T12-T15.","created_at":"2026-06-23T19:54:54","updated_at":"2026-06-23T20:34:42","tags":["data-safety","design","drive","phase2"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef60cfa337b67b372ab4b53e8a4c8","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T12 Core: host.project.open capability (load a .minproj into running Minerva)","description":"MINERVA CORE (repo ~/github/Minerva, branch development — FIRST core change for Drive). Add a host capability host.project.open(path) in CapabilityBroker that validates the path (exists, .minproj) and emits SingletonObject.OpenProject.emit(path) — reusing the File-menu load path (ProjectMenuActions.open_project, incl. the save-current prompt). Register it in the capability enumeration + PluginPolicy grant surface. Headless test: capability returns success + OpenProject emitted (no GUI). Model: Opus direct. Allowed: src/Scripts/Services/Plugins/CapabilityBroker.gd + capability registration sites only. Risks: correct base (development); minimal surface; no scope creep; no PM-in-code. Per T11 design.","created_at":"2026-06-23T19:55:06","updated_at":"2026-06-23T20:52:45","tags":["core","drive","phase2"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef60d0ecb75d8a1137d32648c1e7e","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T13 Drive: open-from-panel (double-click) — pull-latest-then-open, no-clobber","description":"Plugin (minerva-plugins main); uses T12. Panel: Tree.item_activated (double-click) + an Open button -> if the row's file is local & present: pull the latest version of that project first, then call capability:host.project.open(path). If the file is currently open in Minerva AND cloud is newer: do NOT clobber — write cloud to a conflict copy and surface a review (per T11). Record the loaded base (proj_uuid+version). Declare host.project.open in manifest host_capabilities + panel ipc_channels -> REINSTALL. Model: Opus direct (conflict/data-safety correctness). Allowed: drive/ui/DrivePanel.gd, drive/manifest.json, drive/src/main.rs (a pull-then-open helper / minerva_drive_open tool if needed). Risks: DATA SAFETY (no clobber of open file, no lost edit); Godot runtime (item_activated, double-click vs select); value-shapes; reinstall. Per T11.","created_at":"2026-06-23T19:55:11","updated_at":"2026-06-23T20:59:59","tags":["data-safety","drive","phase2"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef60d34567be8978a108a1c0207ad","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T14 Drive: save → push + stale-base divergence handling","description":"Repo per T11 (plugin if hash-on-sync suffices; +Minerva core if a save-hook/event is required). When a tracked .minproj is saved in Minerva, its bytes change -> Drive pushes a new version on next sync (hash-on-sync already detects this). If the cloud advanced since the loaded base -> stale-base divergence -> resolve per T11's policy (recommended: local/open working copy wins canonical path, cloud parked as conflict copy; never lose either side). Decide in T11 whether a core save event is needed for prompt/auto push vs manual Sync. Model: Opus direct. Risks: DATA SAFETY (never lose an edit; never silently overwrite the open file); correct repo+base; DRY (reuse engine). Per T11/T13.","created_at":"2026-06-23T19:55:21","updated_at":"2026-06-23T21:05:00","tags":["data-safety","drive","phase2"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef60d38927fb68ba7db9300d12d9b","type":"work_item","status":"backlog","title":"T15 Core: Open-Recent / File-Open awareness for Drive paths","description":"MINERVA CORE (development). Make Minerva's project-open paths (File>Open and the Open Recent submenu) Drive-aware so the killer scenario is contained: opening a Drive-managed .minproj routes through pull-latest-on-open + a warning when the cloud is ahead; if Drive is not running, show a non-blocking banner \"Drive file — not synced; cloud may be ahead. Start Drive to reconcile.\" Needs core to know a path is Drive-managed (query the Drive plugin, or a marker) — define in T11. Model: Opus direct (trickiest core integration). Allowed: the recent-menu + project-open code paths (menuMain.gd / ProjectMenuActions.gd / app_shell_base.gd) + a Drive-aware hook. Risks: correct base (development); minimal, reversible hook; no scope creep; DATA SAFETY. Per T11.","created_at":"2026-06-23T19:55:22","updated_at":"2026-06-23T21:00:05","tags":["core","data-safety","drive","phase2"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef60d652c7d2cbf149619e20b1e9c","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"T16 Drive: cold-Opus audit of Phase 2 (HITL gate)","description":"Fresh-context Opus audit of all Phase 2 work across BOTH repos (minerva-plugins main + Minerva development) = HITL gate. Tier-A grep gate per task: correct repo+base; allowed-files only; no DCR/ticket/\"user requested\"/meta comments; no duplicated transport/sync/render logic. Tier-B correctness. PLUS the verification additions: (1) cross-boundary value shapes (backend tool JSON matches panel reads; shape tests present); (2) Godot runtime semantics not caught by parse-check (Tree.hide_root, initial fetch in _on_panel_loaded, responsive geometry); (3) deploy/lifecycle correctness (reinstall for manifest/perm changes, /mcp for new tools, binary beside manifest); (4) DATA SAFETY hard gate — prove: never overwrite a file Minerva has open; never lose an edit (conflict copy); pull-latest-on-open; stale-base divergence resolved per the confirmed policy. Run build/test/smoke in both repos. Output GO/NO-GO + findings by severity. Model: Opus, fresh context.","created_at":"2026-06-23T19:55:33","updated_at":"2026-06-23T21:11:04","tags":["audit","drive","gate","phase2"],"parent":"plugins.dct:019ef1535ff77f82ba6665a395388bec"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef66b7c1d753483de88bedbc77bb7","type":"hint","status":"draft","title":"Plugin panel: HFlowContainer wrapping toolbar (not HBox); layout bugs need visual HITL","created_at":"2026-06-23T21:38:19","updated_at":"2026-06-23T21:38:19","tags":["drive","godot","layout","plugins","ui"],"value":"Plugin panel toolbars with several buttons must use HFlowContainer (wraps to new rows when the pane is narrow), NOT HBoxContainer (overflows horizontally and becomes unusable in a narrow editor pane — Minerva panes are a variable grid). Don't wrap the whole panel in a horizontally-non-scrolling ScrollContainer (content keeps its large min width and clips). Pattern that works: root VBox set_anchors_preset(FULL_RECT) + v/h EXPAND_FILL; status/label on its own full-width line; HFlowContainer toolbar; Tree with size_flags_vertical=EXPAND_FILL (fills + scrolls its own rows), small custom_minimum_size. CRITICAL: layout/overflow bugs are NOT caught by --check-only, cargo tests, or headless runs (no rendering) — only a visual HITL catches them. Cheap pre-HITL guard: instantiate the panel against a stub base in a temp project and dump node tree (godot --script) to confirm _build_ui runs + structure, but you still need eyes-on for sizing.","component":"plugins","key":"panel-toolbar-layout","confidence":"high","research_cost":2}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef699c2877129ae0a0dd4ad4c7531","type":"hint","status":"draft","title":"git fetch --tags BEFORE regen_registry.py or registry-check fails (incomplete registry)","created_at":"2026-06-23T22:28:52","updated_at":"2026-06-23T22:28:52","tags":["ci","drive","plugins","registry","release"],"value":"ALWAYS `git fetch --tags origin` before running scripts/regen_registry.py + committing registry.json. regen builds each plugin entry from LOCAL git tags (`git tag -l <id>-v*`, skipping -branch-); the registry-check.yml workflow checks out with fetch-depth:0 (ALL tags) and fails if your committed registry.json differs from its regen. If your local clone is missing some plugins' release tags (never fetched), your regen omits those plugins -> incomplete registry.json -> registry-check FAILS in CI with a drift diff showing the missing entries (hit 2026-06-23: local was missing gen3d-v0.0.1 + movie_gen-v0.0.1, so the drive registry commit dropped them). Correct sequence to release a plugin: push main; tag <id>-v<ver> + push tag; `git fetch --tags`; `python3 scripts/regen_registry.py`; verify the plugin list is COMPLETE (all tagged plugins, not just yours); commit registry.json + push. The marketplace download URLs are deterministic from the tag, so assets can still be building when you regen.","component":"plugins","key":"regen-registry-fetch-tags-first","confidence":"high","research_cost":2}
{"_type":"item","id":"019ef69e22f771949a6282bcd71b480e","type":"hint","status":"draft","title":"Drive on another device: needs development-branch Minerva build + same account; marketplace=imrans-lab","created_at":"2026-06-23T22:33:39","updated_at":"2026-06-23T22:33:39","tags":["cross-device","deploy","drive","marketplace","minerva-build"],"value":"To use Drive on another device: (1) That device's Minerva must be a build from the `development` branch that includes host.project.open (cae1b858, on development only — NOT main). build.yml builds on every push to development and AUTO-CREATES a release each push (auto-build-<timestamp> tags; gate at build.yml:1410 = workflow_dispatch+create_release OR any push) — so grab the newest auto-build release AFTER the relevant dev push. (This corrects stale memory that said create-release was gated to workflow_dispatch — the build workflow was changed.) (2) Marketplace install works because MarketplaceClient.gd:14 REGISTRY_URL_DEFAULT = https://raw.githubusercontent.com/imrans-lab/minerva-plugins/main/registry.json — drive-v0.0.1 is advertised there. (3) Log into the SAME Turnrock account (sync is per-user via host.core.session -> artifact list-mine). Then the project appears as Cloud only; the panel Open button / double-click pulls-then-opens it (no separate Sync needed; handle_open downloads cloud-only into the drive folder, registers, then calls host.project.open). Sync/list/download/reveal/open-externally work without the core capability; only in-app Open needs host.project.open.","component":"drive","key":"cross-device-install-prereqs","confidence":"high","research_cost":2}
{"_type":"item","id":"019f722bbc1b7463b5b83cd19c476026","type":"bug","status":"new","title":"PCB plugin MCP ergonomics: add one-shot load_board + fix tool schemas/docs/naming","description":"## Headline fix — `minerva_pcb_load_board(editor_name, yaml)` (validated against code)\n\nLoading a full canonical board into the editor currently takes ~28 discrete calls (set_board_size + 10× add_component + 15× connect_net + import_footprint_geometry + import_trace_geometry) — and mounting_holes have no MCP ingress at all. Yet both halves of a one-shot load already exist and are tested:\n\n- Go worker `HandleDeserialize` (internal/tools/project.go) parses `yaml`|`minpcb_json` → canonical `board.Board` via `board.UnmarshalYAML`. **Pure function** — returns `{board, warnings}`, no editor side-effect. (This is why the existing `minerva_pcb_pcb_deserialize` tool does NOT load anything into the editor.)\n- GDScript `PCBData.from_board_dict()` (ui/model/pcb_data.gd ~985-1014) rebuilds the full live board from a canonical dict: components, nets, traces, vias, **and** `_load_mounting_holes(...)`. It is the project-file (`pcb.deserialize`) load half.\n\nNew editor-scoped tool composes them:\n```\nminerva_pcb_load_board(editor_name, yaml):\n    board = HandleDeserialize(yaml)      # existing, tested\n    data.from_board_dict(board)          # existing, tested\n    data.data_changed.emit()\n```\nCollapses ~28 calls → 1, loads mounting_holes/pads/traces/vias faithfully, and reuses tested code (DRY). Resolves the \"no bulk load\" and \"mounting_holes have no ingress\" gaps together.\n\n## Other PCB-plugin MCP fixes (from the same session)\n\n- **Under-specified importer schemas.** `import_footprint_geometry.geometry` and `import_trace_geometry.trace_data` are typed as bare `object`; the real required nesting had to be read from source:\n  - geometry: `{components:{<id>:{footprint_found:true, bounding_box:{width,height,center_x,center_y}, pads:[{number,name,type,shape,position:{x,y},size:{width,height},drill,layers}]}}}` (see `pcb_component.gd:load_pad_geometry`).\n  - trace_data: `{traces:[{net_name,layer(\"F.Cu\"/\"B.Cu\"),width,start:{x,y},end:{x,y}}], vias:[{position:{x,y},size,drill,net_name,layers}]}` (see `panel_tools.gd:_import_trace_geometry`).\n  → Put full JSON Schemas in the tools' `inputSchema`.\n\n- **Silent-drop footgun.** A component missing `footprint_found:true` is silently added to `missing_footprints` and skipped; a totally-failed import still returns `success:true`. → Tri-state result (`ok`/`partial`/`error`); route `_import_footprint_geometry` through `_ok`.\n\n- **Footprint enum not exposed.** `add_component.footprint` is validated against `_VALID_FOOTPRINTS` = [RESISTOR, CAPACITOR, IC_DIP, IC_QFP, SWITCH, CONNECTOR, LED, DIODE, TRANSISTOR, HEADER, MOUNTING_HOLE, MODULE]. → Emit as a JSON Schema `enum` on the param.\n\n- **connect_net format mismatch.** Handler wants `pins: [{component, pin}, …]` (panel_tools.gd:_connect_net) but the pcb-maker skill shows `U1.VCC` string form. Also verified: connect_net does NOT require pins to pre-exist (stores membership by name), so the switch A/B ordering concern is a non-issue. → Fix skill + document the dict form.\n\n- **Stale pcb-architect / Docker docs.** `import_*` tool descriptions and the `pcb-maker` skill are written around Docker `pcb-architect`, which the plugin no longer uses (now direct Python libs). → Rewrite descriptions around the data contract; de-Docker the skill. As PCB ejects from Minerva core, the `pcb-maker` skill should move into the plugin.\n\n- **Namespace stutter.** Worker methods `pcb_serialize`/`pcb_deserialize`/`pcb_validate`/… + host `minerva_pcb_` prefix → `minerva_pcb_pcb_*`. Artifact of the ejected native editor. → Drop the redundant `pcb_` from worker method names with a compat-alias window.\n\n## Notes / scope\n\nAll fixes land in minerva-plugins (the plugin), consistent with the in-progress removal of PCB code from Minerva core. Host-wide versions of the schema/envelope/naming/discovery issues are tracked in the Minerva umbrella work-item (MNR).\n\n## Key files\n- internal/tools/project.go (HandleDeserialize / HandleSerialize), internal/board/board.go (UnmarshalYAML), internal/board/minpcb.go\n- ui/model/pcb_data.gd (from_board_dict ~985-1014, _load_mounting_holes)\n- ui/panel_tools.gd (_add_component, _connect_net, _import_footprint_geometry, _import_trace_geometry, _VALID_FOOTPRINTS)\n- ui/model/pcb_component.gd (load_pad_geometry)\n- .claude/skills/pcb-maker (stale Docker/pcb-architect flow)","created_at":"2026-07-17T22:21:36","updated_at":"2026-07-17T23:51:36","priority":2,"severity":3,"tags":["ergonomics","load_board","mcp","pcb","plugin"]}
{"_type":"item","id":"019f812d70e873449d2270c75fa64d7d","type":"bug","status":"new","title":"PCB panel: View control (ratsnest/labels toggles) expands when it should stay fixed-size","created_at":"2026-07-20T20:17:46","updated_at":"2026-07-20T20:17:46","priority":3,"severity":3,"tags":["layout","panel","pcb","ui"],"environment":"Minerva PCB plugin panel; observed while reviewing a route-hint proposal on the smart-remote board.","repro_steps":"1. Open a PCB editor tab.\n2. Observe the View control (ratsnest / labels visibility toggles).\n3. It expands rather than staying at its intrinsic/fixed size."}
{"_type":"item","id":"019f812d901b7c0694811e593c3d5134","type":"bug","status":"new","title":"PCB panel: proposal approve/reject buttons unreachable in wide (2-col, notes-hidden) Minerva layout","created_at":"2026-07-20T20:17:54","updated_at":"2026-07-20T20:17:54","priority":2,"severity":2,"tags":["blocker","layout","pcb","proposals","ui"],"environment":"Minerva wide layout (2-col, notes hidden); PCB editor; smart-remote board.","repro_steps":"1. Set Minerva to wide layout (hide notes -> 2-column window).\n2. Open a PCB editor with an open proposal/route hint.\n3. Try to click the approve/reject buttons — they are off-screen and cannot be reached."}
{"_type":"item","id":"019f812dafe673c79268fa68be98d4e9","type":"bug","status":"new","title":"PCB panel: annotation pane can't be closed in narrow (3-col) layout — open/close button stays in the sidebar and scrolls off-screen","created_at":"2026-07-20T20:18:02","updated_at":"2026-07-20T20:18:02","priority":2,"severity":2,"tags":["annotations","blocker","layout","pcb","ui"],"environment":"Minerva narrow layout (3-col); PCB editor; smart-remote board.","repro_steps":"1. Set Minerva to narrow layout (3-column).\n2. Open the annotation pane in the PCB editor.\n3. Try to close it — the open/close button is in the sidebar and has scrolled off-screen; there is no reachable way to close the pane."}
